{"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Trees"}],"externalID":"Trees","symbolKind":"module","title":"Trees","role":"collection","roleHeading":"Framework"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/AllBinaryTrees","doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Arborescence","doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/BinaryTree","doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Forest","doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/NotATree","doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/OrderedTree","doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/PrefixTree","doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/RootedTree","doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Tree"],"title":"Structures","generated":true,"anchor":"Structures"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/prefixTree(of:)"],"title":"Functions","generated":true,"anchor":"Functions"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/GraphProtocols"],"title":"Extended Modules","generated":true,"anchor":"Extended-Modules"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/trees"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/BinaryTree":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"BinaryTree"}],"title":"BinaryTree","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/BinaryTree","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BinaryTree"}],"url":"\/documentation\/trees\/binarytree","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A binary tree: a rooted tree in which each vertex has at most a left child and a right child,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by position. A vertex with only a left child is a different tree from one with only a right"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"child. Two binary trees are equal when they have the same root and every vertex has the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"left and right children."}]},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/Arborescence":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Arborescence","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Arborescence","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Arborescence","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Arborescence","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/trees\/arborescence","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An arborescence: a directed tree whose edges all point away from its root, so every vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"but the root has exactly one incoming edge, from its parent. As a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successors(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" are the children, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"predecessors(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is the parent (zero or one), and each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedEdge(from: parent, to: child)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/OrderedTree":{"title":"OrderedTree","url":"\/documentation\/trees\/orderedtree","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OrderedTree","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"OrderedTree","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/OrderedTree","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered tree (plane tree): a rooted tree in which the children of each vertex form a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sequence, first to last. The order is part of the value: two ordered trees are equal when they"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"have the same root and every vertex has the same children in the same order, which is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identity being an ordered-tree isomorphism between them."}]},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/trees","title":"Trees","role":"collection","abstract":[],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees"},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/RootedTree":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RootedTree"}],"title":"RootedTree","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/RootedTree","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RootedTree"}],"url":"\/documentation\/trees\/rootedtree","abstract":[{"text":"A tree with a root: an undirected ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"root"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"parent(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"children(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"depth(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and the queries tree algorithms start from. The vertices, edges and their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"positions are the tree’s; the root orders "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"children(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (each vertex’s incident edges in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"position order, without the edge to its parent) and so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"preorder"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/Tree":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Tree"}],"title":"Tree","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Tree","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Tree"}],"url":"\/documentation\/trees\/tree","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A tree: a connected, acyclic undirected graph with at least one vertex, so it has exactly"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"n − 1 edges, no self-loop and no parallel edges. The invariant is the type: every initializer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from unchecked input is failable, and a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tree"},{"type":"text","text":" cannot be mutated."}]},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/NotATree":{"url":"\/documentation\/trees\/notatree","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NotATree"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"NotATree","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The error a checked conversion throws when its input is not one tree, such as a shortest-path"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"forest grown from several sources given to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Arborescence(checked:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NotATree"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/NotATree","type":"topic"},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/GraphProtocols":{"url":"\/documentation\/trees\/graphprotocols","abstract":[],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/GraphProtocols","role":"collection","title":"GraphProtocols","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/Forest":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Forest"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/trees\/forest","abstract":[{"text":"A forest: an acyclic undirected graph, possibly empty, so a disjoint union of trees (an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"isolated vertex is a one-vertex tree). ","type":"text"},{"code":"trees","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lists them by least vertex, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"component(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" says which one a vertex is in."}],"title":"Forest","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Forest","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Forest"}]},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/PrefixTree":{"title":"PrefixTree","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The prefix tree (trie) of some sequences: an arborescence on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<n"},{"type":"text","text":" rooted at 0, the empty"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"prefix, in which each vertex is a distinct prefix of a sequence and each edge appends one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"symbol. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"prefixTree(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" builds it."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/PrefixTree","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PrefixTree","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/trees\/prefixtree","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PrefixTree","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/prefixTree(of:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/trees\/prefixtree(of:)","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"prefixTree(of:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The prefix tree of "},{"code":"sequences","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": one vertex per distinct prefix (the root, 0, is the empty"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one), one edge per vertex but the root, labelled with the symbol it appends, and the vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"where each sequence ends. Repeated sequences end at the same vertex, and an empty sequence at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the root."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"prefixTree"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"